---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'

const lastUpdated = '9 August 2026'

const subprocessors = [
  {
    name: 'Cloudflare, Inc.',
    role: 'Application compute, object storage for evidence records, and transactional email delivery',
    location: 'Provider-operated infrastructure; location depends on the configured service and provider terms',
  },
  {
    name: 'Neon, Inc. (on Amazon Web Services)',
    role: 'Managed Postgres databases holding tenant metadata and evidence sequence state',
    location: 'Provider-operated infrastructure; location depends on the configured service and provider terms',
  },
  {
    name: 'Polar Software, Inc.',
    role: 'Payment and subscription processing (planned — activated when billing goes live)',
    location: 'Provider-operated infrastructure',
  },
]
---
<!-- DRAFT: review with counsel before launch announcement -->

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Veritio"
  description="How Veritio Cloud processes account and security data, our subprocessors, and your data-subject rights under the GDPR."
  claimRefs={['cloud-identity-and-evidence-processing', 'cloud-security-controls', 'cloud-provider-configuration']}
>
  <Nav />

  <main id="main-content">

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink"
        style="font-size: var(--text-headline); line-height: var(--text-headline--line-height);"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        This policy explains what personal data Veritio processes as a
        controller when you use Veritio Cloud — chiefly account and security
        data — how we handle it, and the rights you have. Tenant evidence data
        you send is handled under our Data Processing Agreement, where you are
        the controller.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-muted">
        Draft · Last updated {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line py-14 sm:py-16">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-doc">
        <h2><span class="num">1</span> Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Veritio Cloud is a hosted audit-trail and compliance-evidence service
          operated from Germany. For account and security data described in this
          policy, we act as the data controller under the EU General Data
          Protection Regulation (GDPR).
        </p>

        <p>
          The controller within the meaning of Art. 4(7) GDPR for the personal
          data described in this policy is <strong>Yan Malinovskiy</strong>
          (sole proprietor), Belchenstraße&nbsp;2, 79276 Reute, Germany,
          <a href="mailto:hello@getveritio.com">hello@getveritio.com</a>.
          No Data Protection Officer is appointed; the thresholds of
          Art. 37 GDPR and § 38 BDSG are not met at the current scale of
          processing. Direct all privacy inquiries to the controller at the
          address above. See also the <a href="/legal/imprint/">Imprint</a>.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">2</span> Two roles: controller and processor</h2>
        <p>
          It matters which data we mean. For the personal data in your
          <strong>account</strong> — the data needed to run the service and keep
          it secure — Veritio is the <strong>controller</strong>, and this policy
          governs it. For the <strong>evidence records</strong> your applications
          and agents send into your tenant, Veritio is a <strong>processor</strong>
          acting on your instructions; you are the controller of that data, and
          our <a href="/legal/dpa/">Data Processing Agreement</a> governs it.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">3</span> Account data we process</h2>
        <p>As controller, we process:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Identity and contact data</strong> — your email address, your
            name if you provide it, and your membership in an organization —
            processed to create and operate your account, verify your email, send
            team invitations, and communicate with you about the service.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Authentication data</strong> — a securely hashed password and
            email-verification state — processed to authenticate you and protect
            your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Security audit data</strong> — including IP addresses and
            timestamps of sign-in and sensitive account actions — processed to
            detect and investigate abuse, secure the service, and keep a security
            record. We keep this to what is needed for that purpose.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Billing data</strong> — once billing is live, subscription and
            payment status. Card details are handled by our payment processor,
            Polar, and are not stored by Veritio.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Consistent with how the product is designed, we prefer stable
          identifiers over unnecessary personal data and do not seek freeform
          personal data we do not need.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">4</span> Why we process it (legal bases)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Performance of a contract</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) — to
            provide the service under our Terms, including creating your account,
            authenticating you, and handling invitations and billing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) — to secure
            the service, prevent and investigate abuse, and keep security audit
            records, balanced against your rights.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal obligation</strong> (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR) — to meet
            retention, tax, and lawful-request obligations that apply to us.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2><span class="num">5</span> Subprocessors</h2>
        <p>
          We use a small set of infrastructure providers to run the service. Each
          is bound by data-protection terms, and each processes data only to
          provide its part of the service.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Provider</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Location</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                subprocessors.map((s) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>{s.name}</td>
                    <td>{s.role}</td>
                    <td>{s.location}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          We maintain this list current and give notice of material changes as
          described in the <a href="/legal/dpa/">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">6</span> International processing</h2>
        <p>
          The service uses the subprocessors listed above. Their processing
          locations depend on the services configured for the account and their
          applicable terms. Where a transfer of personal data outside the EEA
          requires safeguards, we rely on an available lawful transfer mechanism,
          including Standard Contractual Clauses where applicable. This public
          policy does not promise a specific storage region unless that
          commitment appears in a separate signed agreement.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">7</span> Cookies &amp; website analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Veritio Cloud uses only strictly necessary cookies to keep you signed in
          and to secure the session. We do not use advertising cookies or
          cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          On this website (getveritio.com) we measure aggregate traffic with
          <strong>Umami</strong> (Umami Software, Inc., EU-hosted). Umami is
          cookieless and stores no personal identifiers; we see only aggregate
          statistics such as page views, referrers, and approximate location
          derived from your IP address (country and city — the IP address
          itself is not stored).
        </p>
        <p>
          With your consent — asked once via the cookie banner — we additionally
          use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google Ireland Limited, with
          Google LLC in the US as sub-processor under the EU-US Data Privacy
          Framework). Google Analytics sets cookies and processes usage data to
          report how visitors use the site. It does not load unless you accept,
          and you can withdraw consent at any time via &ldquo;Cookie
          settings&rdquo; in the footer. Withdrawal updates Google consent to
          denied and removes the site's Google Analytics cookies. Google may
          still receive cookieless consent-status pings after the tag has
          loaded; no Google Analytics tag is requested before you accept.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">8</span> Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep account data for as long as your account is active and for a
          limited period afterward to meet legal obligations and resolve disputes,
          then delete or de-identify it. Security audit data is kept only as long
          as needed for security and legal purposes. Retention of tenant evidence
          data is governed by your instructions and the
          <a href="/legal/dpa/">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">9</span> Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Subject to applicable law, you have the right to access, rectify, erase,
          restrict, and port your personal data, to object to processing based on
          legitimate interests, and to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
          authority. Where we act as processor for tenant evidence data, please
          direct data-subject requests to the customer who controls that tenant;
          we will assist that customer as described in the Data Processing
          Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">10</span> Not legal advice</h2>
        <p class="emphatic">
          Veritio supports compliance evidence workflows. It does not provide
          legal advice and does not guarantee that your use of the service is
          compliant with the GDPR or any other framework.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">11</span> Contact</h2>
        <p>
          To exercise a right or ask a privacy question, contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@getveritio.com">hello@getveritio.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-doc {
    --measure: 70ch;
  }
  .legal-doc h2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .legal-doc h2 .num {
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    transform: translateY(0.15em);
  }
  .legal-doc p,
  .legal-doc li {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .legal-doc ul {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .legal-doc li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .legal-doc li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.72em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .legal-doc strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .legal-doc a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .legal-doc a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
  }
  .legal-doc .emphatic {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-evergreen);
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .legal-doc .table-wrap {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .legal-doc table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 560px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .legal-doc th {
    padding: 10px 16px 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: bottom;
  }
  .legal-doc td {
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 13px 16px 13px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .legal-doc td:first-child {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
